# The build context is sent to the daemon in full before anything runs. Without this it was
# 432 MB and took 82 seconds, because it carried both trees' node_modules and their build output.
#
# Size is the smaller problem. The real one: `COPY apps/api/ ./` runs AFTER `npm ci` in the build
# stage, so a node_modules in the context overwrites the freshly installed Linux dependencies with
# whatever the host had -- on Windows, native binaries that cannot execute in the image. The image
# would build and then fail at runtime, which is the expensive kind of wrong.

**/node_modules
**/dist
**/.env
**/.env.*
!**/.env.example

# Generated by `prisma generate` inside the image, from the schema. A host copy would be stale.
apps/api/src/generated

# Nothing in the image needs these, and they change on every commit, busting the layer cache.
.git
.github
docs
**/*.tsbuildinfo
**/coverage
**/.vscode
**/.idea
